    family-names: Praditiansyah
    email: kevinpradithh@gmail.com
repository-code: https://github.com/kevinpradith/convert.in
url: https://github.com/kevinpradith/convert.in
abstract: >-
  Image and PDF tools that never upload a file. A browser application and a
  command line tool share one isomorphic core, so a change lands in both at
  once. Images convert between PNG, JPEG, WebP, AVIF and JPEG XL through
  WebAssembly codecs; PDFs are built, merged, reordered, split, stamped,
  signed, compressed to a size limit, stripped of their metadata, redacted by
  rebuilding the pages from pixels, and encrypted with AES-256 written as the
  ISO 32000-2 revision 6 handler. The claim that nothing leaves the machine is
  enforced by a Content-Security-Policy and checked by a browser suite that
  fails if a single request leaves the origin.
keywords:
  - pdf
  - image-processing
  - privacy
  - local-first
  - offline
  - webassembly
  - pdf-encryption
  - redaction
